{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:21:31.835071Z","id":"b0f1d8ab693a9733f308ebd6cccae0068f42363f9bcf97ecb0d724b404fa7bc0","body":{"detail":"CI's worker job runs scripts/check-wasm.sh and just worker-test natively, outside scripts/bazel-test.sh --ci, so just ci stays Bazel-only and makes no target/ or node_modules in a worktree. Under Bazel it would need a wasm32-unknown-unknown platform for rules_rust, a C toolchain whose clang targets wasm32 for bundled SQLite (rusqlite's sqlite-wasm-rs), crates/clax-worker's own Cargo.lock in crate_universe, worker-build (crates/clax-worker/build.sh installs it with cargo install) and wrangler from npm. Until then a local just ci does not run them; just check-wasm and just worker-test do.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":81},"end":{"line":117},"content_hash":"f75be890b6096e95cba144280fc77498d29f12bed337bdff3b9c0e486005b53e"},"summary":"Build crates/clax-worker and check the Worker's crates for wasm32 under Bazel","tags":["build","ci","revisit:rules_rust builds a wasm32 target with a C toolchain here, or a wasm32 break reaches main past the worker job","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:36:33.910414Z","id":"38985b9c78838e41be333a059185193c8479f029c7b59b504b5f6175c8cad1cf","body":{"detail":"CI's worker job runs scripts/check-wasm.sh and just worker-test natively, outside scripts/bazel-test.sh --ci, so just ci stays Bazel-only and makes no target/ or node_modules in a worktree. Under Bazel it would need a wasm32-unknown-unknown platform for rules_rust, a C toolchain whose clang targets wasm32 for bundled SQLite (rusqlite's sqlite-wasm-rs), crates/clax-worker's own Cargo.lock in crate_universe, worker-build (crates/clax-worker/build.sh installs it with cargo install) and wrangler from npm. Until then a local just ci does not run them; just check-wasm and just worker-test do.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":81},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"62cd0c2a7a506af02bc95d2e2b3d3f415b7b4811c74ea0183bd34e08aa55b1e9"},"summary":"Build crates/clax-worker and check the Worker's crates for wasm32 under Bazel","supersedes":"b0f1d8ab693a9733f308ebd6cccae0068f42363f9bcf97ecb0d724b404fa7bc0","tags":["build","ci","revisit:rules_rust builds a wasm32 target with a C toolchain here, or a wasm32 break reaches main past the worker job","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:36:33.972449Z","id":"c62c963e7d79bef354f0611d2b1bffbc1499018245c6dc902126cf2613e2ccd3","body":{"detail":"web/BUILD.bazel declares //web:playwright with the @playwright/test package's generated playwright_binary, replacing a js_binary whose entry point inside the linked package failed analysis on every platform (\"is a prefix of the other\", CI run 39153903425). On macOS it builds and `bazelisk run //web:playwright -- --version` prints Version 1.63.0, and scripts/bazel-test.sh --ci now builds it. install-deps itself installs Chromium's system libraries with apt through sudo, which only the ubuntu-latest runner does; the first CI run of this workflow shows whether it works there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":33},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"2e92564feb69742457763f8603190b484513b992dfce20a47e06c9bb9e1111bd"},"summary":"`bazelisk run //web:playwright -- install-deps chromium` has not run on the Linux runner since //web:playwright became rules_js's playwright_binary","tags":["ci","bazel","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:01:15.875843Z","id":"2859273ed74d296293bd9b4093dd5aa4ea3ca1792d4db68a9e5f35b076a6afb6","body":{"detail":"scripts/bazel-test.sh --ci tests tests(//...) except manual, which now takes in //apps/clax_app's test files, :dart_analyze, :apk_test (the APK: Flutter's Linux engine and gen_snapshot, the Linux NDK r28c and build tools 36.0.0 pinned in MODULE.bazel, the Go toolchain, the Maven libraries) and //crates/clax-cli:clax_android_*; :macos_app_test is macOS only (target_compatible_with). All of it was built and run on macOS (arm64) only, on 2026-10-17; the Linux pins' checksums were computed from the downloads but never used by a build. The runner's cache (6 GB, .github/actions/setup-bazel) and time will also grow: the NDK and SDK archives alone are about 1 GB.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"15e213b0a3e70d43d9c3cac0874a5973b98528eaaa01d8e613bbdad321114f8f"},"summary":"CI's Linux runner now builds and tests the Clax app, which was only run on macOS","tags":["ci","unverified","linux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:27:54.171344Z","id":"5cfa29c1e943b6a3a8191a95b490ef3655053885e50b0ac2f012645354ca848b","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"2859273ed74d296293bd9b4093dd5aa4ea3ca1792d4db68a9e5f35b076a6afb6","summary":"//crates/clax-cli:clax_android_* are deleted (49a0cccabd27); the Android code CI builds for the app is now //crates/clax-embed:clax_embed_android_{arm64,x86_64} and :android_symbols_test.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/publish-pi.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:03:55.566044Z","id":"d8862507094b924f83798d71c52fd21afc4efebf7e999671e0316e185dae4882","body":{"detail":"Failure: a user with write access pushes a branch whose publish-pi.yml drops this step (or checks out any commit) and runs `gh workflow run publish-pi.yml --ref that-branch -f dry_run=false`; workflow_dispatch runs the workflow file at that ref (https://docs.github.com/en/actions/writing-workflows/choosing-what-your-workflow-does/events-that-trigger-workflows#workflow_dispatch), the job gets an OIDC token (id-token: write), and npm accepts it because a trusted publisher configured as scripts/release.sh:678-681 and docs/usage.md print it ('no environment') matches on repository and workflow filename only. The check guards against mistakes, not against an unreviewed commit being published.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":61},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"8cb5391f3658c557a7e10550b0a97d7202f73e75328c272f5542ee6a447974b0"},"suggested_fix":"Give the publish job a GitHub environment (e.g. npm) whose deployment branches allow only main, and print/document that environment for the npm trusted-publisher setup, so npm refuses tokens from runs on other refs.","summary":"The on-main and CI-passed check is bypassable by anyone who can dispatch: the workflow runs from the dispatched ref, and the trusted publisher names no environment","tags":["review","review:release-script-2","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/publish-pi.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:03:55.566070Z","id":"f98bbcc12e690b22ab75a2ab1ca1b48e45c5d5016f01b899fad51d373251f7de","body":{"detail":"Failure: on a push to main, ci.yml's perf-log job (.github/workflows/ci.yml:125-134) joins concurrency group perf-log; when a third push queues behind a running one, GitHub cancels the pending one (https://docs.github.com/en/actions/writing-workflows/choosing-what-your-workflow-does/control-the-concurrency-of-workflows-and-jobs), so the release's pin or merge commit gets conclusion 'cancelled' though its bazel gate passed. This step then refuses the publish, and scripts/release.sh:622-627 (step 13) fails the same way; even uncancelled, step 13 waits for the benchmarks (timeout 60 min each, queued behind earlier ones) within its 90-minute poll budget.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":75},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"ddb39cd4f10ec443d61e1d88e90da05962df7d7748990f346ab37a5b21d4b656"},"suggested_fix":"Judge the bazel job's conclusion (gh run view <id> --json jobs) rather than the run's, in both this check and release.sh's step 13 wait.","summary":"'CI passed' is the whole ci.yml run's conclusion, which includes the perf-log job: a cancelled perf run refuses the publish","tags":["review","review:release-script-2","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/publish-pi.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:05:39.188902Z","id":"51e747beb589c25b3828bd3bbc9733b42916715b53575dcb99042fcb35e7dc06","body":{"detail":".github/workflows/publish-pi.yml:22-32 triggers on workflow_dispatch only; :46-56 gives the publish job id-token: write and no `environment:`. scripts/release.sh:678-681 prints the trusted-publisher setup with 'no environment'. workflow_dispatch runs the workflow file from the chosen ref (https://docs.github.com/en/actions/writing-workflows/choosing-what-your-workflow-does/events-that-trigger-workflows#workflow_dispatch), and npm's trusted publisher matches on owner, repository, workflow filename and an optional environment (https://docs.npmjs.com/trusted-publishers), so a branch copy of publish-pi.yml without the check at :61-80 can publish. Kind concern is right: it takes someone with write access.","kind":"comment","references":"d8862507094b924f83798d71c52fd21afc4efebf7e999671e0316e185dae4882","summary":"confirmed: the on-main/CI check lives in the dispatched ref's workflow file, and the job has no environment to bind the trusted publisher to main","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/publish-pi.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:05:39.189046Z","id":"b89c1558e03b947a7f40d9381f82f22c41cbc38ed4ccc6b355d380127e7f3838","body":{"detail":".github/workflows/publish-pi.yml:75-80 requires `.[0].conclusion == success` for the ci.yml push run. scripts/release.sh:622-627 (step_13) waits via await_run, which accepts only 'completed success' (scripts/release.sh:529-534). .github/workflows/ci.yml:126-140 adds perf-log on pushes to main (needs: bazel, timeout-minutes: 60, concurrency group perf-log, cancel-in-progress: false). GitHub cancels an already pending job in a concurrency group when another queues, whatever cancel-in-progress says (https://docs.github.com/en/actions/writing-workflows/choosing-what-your-workflow-does/control-the-concurrency-of-workflows-and-jobs), so the run concludes 'cancelled' and both gates refuse.","kind":"comment","references":"f98bbcc12e690b22ab75a2ab1ca1b48e45c5d5016f01b899fad51d373251f7de","summary":"confirmed: both gates read the whole ci.yml run's conclusion, which includes the perf-log job","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/publish-pi.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:21:06.112364Z","id":"02977601a148bea47a5f8902ae7901801aba6ca36c690a53dde002d549c853a6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d4f3ff246","summary":"publish-pi.yml's job runs in the GitHub environment npm, which the trusted publisher names (release.sh's printed setup, docs/usage.md and the workflow header now say environment npm); release.sh reads the environment read-only and warns in a dry run, refuses a release, when it is missing or allows more than main, printing the settings to make. Evidence: //scripts:release_script PASSED at 4fde7462c (bazelisk test, 63 checks), cases 'a dry run warns that the npm environment is missing, with the steps to make it', 'preflight refuses a release with no npm environment', 'an npm environment open to every branch', 'an npm environment for another branch'. Creating the environment remains the owner's repository setting.","supersedes":"d8862507094b924f83798d71c52fd21afc4efebf7e999671e0316e185dae4882","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/publish-pi.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:21:06.139262Z","id":"bb41302c29ca205ee4149bc8fd3baffa8aecc59b536a3bacb31aefbb33e79968","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5b6825592","summary":"publish-pi.yml reads the conclusion of ci.yml's bazel job (gh run view --json jobs), and release.sh's step 13 waits for that job alone (ci_gate_state), not perf-log. Evidence: //scripts:release_script PASSED at 4fde7462c; its fake gh reports run 201 as 'completed cancelled' as a whole, and the full-run and resume cases pass on the bazel job's state.","supersedes":"f98bbcc12e690b22ab75a2ab1ca1b48e45c5d5016f01b899fad51d373251f7de","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T20:43:54.594941Z","id":"a76e764550eac739046557ad760f5fd11dd48130bbe72fec210d1f3c487747d0","body":{"detail":"Why the native tests and clippy stay outside Bazel too is the alternative recorded on crates/clax-worker/BUILD.bazel:1:35.","kind":"comment","references":"38985b9c78838e41be333a059185193c8479f029c7b59b504b5f6175c8cad1cf","summary":"The Worker's format check is now under Bazel (//crates/clax-worker:rustfmt, crates/clax-worker/BUILD.bazel); its tests, clippy, wasm build and e2e stay in the worker job (scripts/worker-checks.sh), as this alternative describes.","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/release.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:26:26.947222Z","id":"f24d6f3407afd12a98aa51bf9e80cdd5af84345e0765473756f59af03d7fb039","body":{"detail":"Every other build job runs on Blacksmith. Blacksmith offers no Intel Mac, and scripts/smoke-release-binary.sh runs the built binary, which on an arm64 Mac needs Rosetta; whether Blacksmith's macOS image has it is unverified. GitHub's macos-15-intel runs it natively.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":82},"content_hash":"9ec025906e3aa3c5d0cdaf0a131e8bc14f37a7dab08dfd3e9e233a5c42d1026f"},"summary":"Build x86_64-apple-darwin on Blacksmith's arm64 Mac, cross-compiled, instead of GitHub's macos-15-intel","tags":["ci","release","revisit:Blacksmith offers an Intel Mac, or its arm64 macOS image is shown to run x86_64 binaries under Rosetta","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:28:16.380923Z","id":"1a7c6091e6021d9d378bd2f5348a9f9a1131fed588991df19e00b08052acc511","body":{"detail":"web/BUILD.bazel declares //web:playwright with the @playwright/test package's generated playwright_binary, replacing a js_binary whose entry point inside the linked package failed analysis on every platform (\"is a prefix of the other\", CI run 39153903425). On macOS it builds and `bazelisk run //web:playwright -- --version` prints Version 1.63.0, and scripts/bazel-test.sh --ci now builds it. install-deps itself installs Chromium's system libraries with apt through sudo, which only the ubuntu-latest runner does; the first CI run of this workflow shows whether it works there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":39},"end":{"line":42},"content_hash":"2e92564feb69742457763f8603190b484513b992dfce20a47e06c9bb9e1111bd"},"summary":"`bazelisk run //web:playwright -- install-deps chromium` has not run on the Linux runner since //web:playwright became rules_js's playwright_binary","supersedes":"c62c963e7d79bef354f0611d2b1bffbc1499018245c6dc902126cf2613e2ccd3","tags":["ci","bazel","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:28:16.409927Z","id":"52acd676f79e9d4cc166f5371c1927093a031d223776cd9744478959483024ab","body":{"detail":"CI's worker job runs scripts/check-wasm.sh and just worker-test natively, outside scripts/bazel-test.sh --ci, so just ci stays Bazel-only and makes no target/ or node_modules in a worktree. Under Bazel it would need a wasm32-unknown-unknown platform for rules_rust, a C toolchain whose clang targets wasm32 for bundled SQLite (rusqlite's sqlite-wasm-rs), crates/clax-worker's own Cargo.lock in crate_universe, worker-build (crates/clax-worker/build.sh installs it with cargo install) and wrangler from npm. Until then a local just ci does not run them; just check-wasm and just worker-test do.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":98},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"f8c56ba226211acac03a443675fc68cf8f2b95623d688a9fd761579ecfacb352"},"summary":"Build crates/clax-worker and check the Worker's crates for wasm32 under Bazel","supersedes":"38985b9c78838e41be333a059185193c8479f029c7b59b504b5f6175c8cad1cf","tags":["build","ci","revisit:rules_rust builds a wasm32 target with a C toolchain here, or a wasm32 break reaches main past the worker job","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T03:41:50.268806Z","id":"1df2c4f47183a75ba844f3ee9460e019b506816fc2108367c6e19fbd3e91a305","body":{"detail":"The disk is last-writer-wins. If run A's bazel job fails and its bazel-seed commits after run B's green bazel job, later runs start from A's state. Bazel's content-addressed caching keeps results correct; only speed suffers, since B's changes are rebuilt. A workflow concurrency group for pushes to main would serialise runs, but it also cancels pending runs, and scripts/release.sh waits for the bazel job on its pin commit, so it is not done.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":75},"end":{"line":77},"content_hash":"8ade8dc5425711e89b98bcac61bc2f5b82ee3d965d37b57930aeb2660bc75972"},"summary":"Two pushes to main close together can leave the disk at the older commit's state","tags":["revisit:if-ci-runs-on-main-are-often-slow-after-close-pushes","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:01:33.169013Z","id":"f350787eb171da64364409d4f1037dfaa76bcb0adabd51f6579c7ad12f1288ba","body":{"detail":"Seen across CI's eight pushes to main before f57ec462b, each failing on code that passed on other runs: //apps/clax_app:agent_worker_test (2 of 8), //apps/clax_app:remote_push_pull_real_test (1 of 8), //web:unit (2 of 8), the Rust integration shard integration__6 in api_claxbot_run (1 of 8); single e2e failures contract.spec.ts:224 and user-assets.spec.ts:38 (job 120937366756), app-mode.spec.ts:307 and home-app.spec.ts:73 (job 120582395724), app-mode.spec.ts:346 (job 120610193386). The bazel-seed job prints \"not all targets were analyzed\" on every run. None was reproduced or traced.","kind":"concern","summary":"Intermittent failures on main not yet traced: agent_worker_test, remote_push_pull_real_test, web:unit, integration__6 (api_claxbot_run), single e2e tests, and bazel-seed's analysis warning","tags":["ci","flaky","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T12:53:28.922487Z","id":"3683a6576bee25c22f480e6c8a3e9e3302e3f79e846f8b0ab478510df5378750","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f350787eb171da64364409d4f1037dfaa76bcb0adabd51f6579c7ad12f1288ba","summary":"Three of CI run 40635079996's failures traced: bot-offer.test.ts:53 (dynamic import of ./bot/api outlasting settle(), fixed in 55c692830), ask-where.spec.ts:102 (inbox summary race, record 9d2a17e0, fixed in c8b307ed1), drag-release.spec.ts:55 (layout-hovered mouse under Linux Chromium, record 71e69921, test changed in 4d4028bc4). Still untraced, each failing once on macOS under just test-affected main at 93816ec34 and passing on rerun: chrome-overlay.spec.ts:897 ('Frame has been detached' at frameElement, line 914), inspect-tests.spec.ts:146 (404 on docs/ticks/t at fixtures.ts:174), working.spec.ts:32 (strict-mode violation: two '.chip.ag' in the Working card), and an e2e daemon that did not become healthy (fixtures.ts:79). A rerun of //web:e2e_rest and //web:e2e_chrome_overlay alone, and --repeat-each=6 of ask-where:102, drag-release:55, working:32 and inspect-tests:146 (48 passed), did not reproduce them.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:22:00.892523Z","id":"c936555e1a53cc25184804126f60c4b053df4d4897e95bd2480026ac3d68489b","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f350787eb171da64364409d4f1037dfaa76bcb0adabd51f6579c7ad12f1288ba","summary":"Traced on branch fix-main-ci: bazel-seed's analysis failure (Apple-only tests requested explicitly on Linux without --skip_incompatible_explicit_targets; fixed in 48ebdbf2f), agent_worker_test's late-answers test (untracked asked.json writes outlasting until's turn budget; 33909e51e), app-mode.spec.ts:321 (a back() report overtaken by the next back() re-pushed onto the trail in web/shell/src/app/host.ts; 0d6d589b0, unit test in host.test.ts), and inspect-tests.spec.ts:146 (totalMs: 300 spent loading migrate.js before the first write; 3000 ms plus a poll in 0f? see git log -- web/e2e/inspect-tests.spec.ts; remaining real-time dependence is record 198a9929). api_hosted an_admins_export_holds_their_own_search_words_alone (503 export_busy from a second export sent while the first body streamed) was fixed on main in d19de548d. working.spec.ts:32's strict-mode violation was fixed on main by picking the gallery card by its link.","tags":["session:claude-code:3e8d3518-726a-4423-93d1-4f827624829c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:22:12.891619Z","id":"1e219706821fb166222f286d7dc6224e13d6abb0d61f96f172b17283d8064f2a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f350787eb171da64364409d4f1037dfaa76bcb0adabd51f6579c7ad12f1288ba","summary":"Traced on branch fix-main-ci: bazel-seed's analysis failure (Apple-only tests requested explicitly on Linux without --skip_incompatible_explicit_targets; fixed in 48ebdbf2f), agent_worker_test's late-answers test (untracked asked.json writes outlasting until's turn budget; 33909e51e), app-mode.spec.ts:321 (a back() report overtaken by the next back() re-pushed onto the trail in web/shell/src/app/host.ts; 0d6d589b0, unit test in web/shell/src/app/host.test.ts), and inspect-tests.spec.ts:146 (totalMs: 300 spent loading migrate.js before the first write; 3000 ms and a poll for the first write in c6ff68f96; its remaining real-time dependence is record 198a9929). api_hosted::an_admins_export_holds_their_own_search_words_alone (503 export_busy from a second export sent while the first body streamed) was fixed on main in d19de548d. working.spec.ts:32's strict-mode violation was fixed on main by picking the gallery card by its link.","supersedes":"c936555e1a53cc25184804126f60c4b053df4d4897e95bd2480026ac3d68489b","tags":["session:claude-code:3e8d3518-726a-4423-93d1-4f827624829c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T22:30:26.709184Z","id":"7d42e12c9aed71a62996af853c5f026b41e9be52c099781933a92a658e394cca","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f350787eb171da64364409d4f1037dfaa76bcb0adabd51f6579c7ad12f1288ba","summary":"Traced on branch fix-main-ci. Fixed: bazel-seed's analysis failure (Apple-only tests requested explicitly on Linux without --skip_incompatible_explicit_targets; 48ebdbf2f); agent_worker_test's late-answers test (untracked asked.json writes outlasting until's turn budget; 33909e51e); inspect-tests.spec.ts:146 (totalMs: 300 spent loading migrate.js before the first write; c6ff68f96, its remaining real-time dependence is record 198a9929); //web:unit failing with every test passing (reportChrome's timer, Node's under vitest, firing after bridge-migrate.test.ts's window was torn down; a0f7d1f47); subpages.spec.ts:146 (the greet after Back depends on whether the page's first hello came before its first load, frame-gate.ts; e8f7036d8, the CI order inferred, not observed); app_background_test's five make tests (60 x 10 ms budget for PendingMake's real writes; 8d3f95170); api_people::a_waiting_agent_takes_with_its_narrowed_rights (the narrowed take answers at once with a no_access placeholder, so waiting for the poll to wait raced it; 5cfaf4b2a, reproduced 1 in 300 and 300 of 300 after). Not fixed: app-mode.spec.ts:321 failed again on CI run 40771210341 at line 357 after 0d6d589b0, which fixes one real race (unit test in web/shell/src/app/host.test.ts) but not the CI failure; not reproduced in 120 local runs; 5196fb1ad makes the test write trail.json (the page's reports and the host's posts) to its output folder on failure. Fixed on main earlier: api_hosted an_admins_export_holds_their_own_search_words_alone (d19de548d) and working.spec.ts:32.","supersedes":"1e219706821fb166222f286d7dc6224e13d6abb0d61f96f172b17283d8064f2a","tags":["session:claude-code:3e8d3518-726a-4423-93d1-4f827624829c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/deploy-prod.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:17:34.252736Z","id":"e498f883a0f645da4d1673877c0565f60ddd23a0715429c1dc21ceef4b90f594","body":{"detail":"The deploy job restores no cache, so each deploy compiles the Worker and its dependencies and installs every package from scratch: a job holding the Cloudflare token runs nothing a cache could have planted. Swatinem/rust-cache and setup-node's pnpm cache, keyed to prod, would shorten it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":51},"end":{"line":63},"content_hash":"0baa3cc2218293e68004b7578a942664369b66f53b90f239f4c28cde49d61422"},"summary":"Cache the Rust build and pnpm store in the deploy job","tags":["revisit:a deploy takes long enough that time from merge to live matters","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/deploy-prod.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:17:34.252770Z","id":"39266820edbd5fddf3aeb1c54d0d2f29f9ae3e1116fc7bb747953a8a54469ed1","body":{"detail":"The production environment's variables are not readable from the drift job (the environment admits prod only; scheduled runs are on main), so the job uses vars.PUBLIC_HOST at repository level, defaulting to clax.dev. An instance on another host needs that repository variable set by hand.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":119},"end":{"line":128},"content_hash":"2d2e42f6ef7ffd53bae9e8b322378289a21227d318c7c53baff42c6b9ffed0bc"},"summary":"The drift job reads the repository variable PUBLIC_HOST, which scripts/setup-prod-github.sh does not set","tags":["config","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/deploy-prod.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:22:47.683306Z","id":"2c506ca49f617f70765aad2a07e7cad4bf38fe0ffdffc72a67c01f68de06df29","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d43e9f18b","summary":"scripts/setup-prod-github.sh step 4 now sets the repository variable PUBLIC_HOST (created, PATCHed when different, else left); //scripts:setup_prod_github passes, with its cases 'the repository variable PUBLIC_HOST is clax.dev, for the drift check' and '--public-host updates the environment's and the repository's PUBLIC_HOST' (31 PASS)","supersedes":"39266820edbd5fddf3aeb1c54d0d2f29f9ae3e1116fc7bb747953a8a54469ed1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/deploy-prod.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:41:56.976807Z","id":"24dc2571e2b22b992aae0effd6cc7c5bb6fc7cf4f5d0eb2146eadf4c336f7eaa","body":{"detail":"The secrets are set on the one step that runs scripts/cloudflare-setup.sh, and that script runs pnpm install (web/), npm ci (crates/clax-worker, whose dependencies include wrangler and its install scripts) at scripts/cloudflare-setup.sh:203-205, then deploy.mjs runs `cargo install worker-build@0.8.7` (crates/clax-worker/build.sh:10-12) and the wasm build, whose build.rs scripts all run before the upload. Every one of those processes inherits both tokens. They are pinned by lockfiles and crates.io versions, so this is a supply-chain exposure, not a known hole; but the account-wide Workers Scripts: Edit token (docs/prod.md:78-87) is the most powerful credential the repository holds.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":91},"content_hash":"5ea91762d2d04788a0c7e3499ef83246b1875c0c9240975f66e829a058e55422"},"suggested_fix":"Install and build in steps with no secrets (cloudflare-setup.sh --ci without --i-know-what-i-am-doing builds and ends at wrangler deploy --dry-run, or a separate build step), then deploy with deploy.mjs --no-build in a step that alone gets the secrets.","summary":"The deploy step's environment holds CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN and CLAX_SMOKE_TOKEN while it installs and builds third-party code","tags":["review","review:prod-releases","security","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/deploy-prod.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:41:56.977202Z","id":"0932d6a221651f3b40f3420b68c7415e46371cf5732a99baad99c5280a4a6c80","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-prod-releases-design.md (Workflows, deploy-prod.yml) says the deploy writes the commit, build and Cloudflare version to the job summary. The Summary step reads only the record's `build` (deploy.mjs's record has no Worker version ID: crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs's `next` record) and the /healthz body. Without the version ID, rolling back with `wrangler rollback <version>` starts with looking it up in the dashboard.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":93},"end":{"line":113},"content_hash":"6a090bcd0eca105ad6387dbb81863cac58fb6702849068f445b3119e58ebb1ab"},"suggested_fix":"Have deploy.mjs keep the version ID wrangler deploy prints (\"Current Version ID: …\") in the record, and print it in the summary; or drop the item from the design.","summary":"The job summary gives the commit, the build and /healthz, but not the Cloudflare version the design asks for","tags":["review","review:prod-releases","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/deploy-prod.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T19:57:31.907565Z","id":"92da09d553b88825cf50d29ca94d6ef0301c53045dea4c89df99e683d7708c21","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"24dc2571e2b22b992aae0effd6cc7c5bb6fc7cf4f5d0eb2146eadf4c336f7eaa","summary":"Confirmed: .github/workflows/deploy-prod.yml:65-91 is one step whose env holds CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN and CLAX_SMOKE_TOKEN and runs scripts/cloudflare-setup.sh, which runs scripts/pnpm-install-stamped.sh web and scripts/npm-ci-stamped.sh crates/clax-worker (scripts/cloudflare-setup.sh:203-205), then deploy.mjs's build (crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs:835-842: scripts/build-web.sh, then build.sh, whose `cargo install worker-build@0.8.7` and build scripts run in that environment).","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/deploy-prod.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T19:57:31.907961Z","id":"a97b012bd1a1ccd08349b84d54f762327aad976fca9140088b3685ee04e5ace8","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0932d6a221651f3b40f3420b68c7415e46371cf5732a99baad99c5280a4a6c80","summary":"Confirmed: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-prod-releases-design.md:129 names the Cloudflare version in the job summary; the record deploy.mjs writes (crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs:899-917, `next`) has no version field, and the Summary step (deploy-prod.yml:95-113) prints only the commit, `build` and /healthz.","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/deploy-prod.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T20:08:13.301281Z","id":"ae51c3a2a1709a30eeb2de06e9d382b1cb4691c886374a1e280e8228d40053cb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3d0e9dcd5","summary":"Fixed: .github/workflows/deploy-prod.yml's 'Build' step, whose env has no secret, runs scripts/cloudflare-setup.sh --ci --production as a dry run (installs, builds the web UI and the Worker with CLAX_BUILD_COMMIT from the commit, ends at wrangler deploy --dry-run); the 'Deploy' step alone gets CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN and CLAX_SMOKE_TOKEN and passes --no-build, which skips the package installs in cloudflare-setup.sh and makes deploy.mjs refuse a build/index_bg.wasm that is missing or does not embed HEAD (deploy-lib.mjs builtFromRefusal). Evidence: node --test crates/clax-worker/deploy-lib.test.mjs passes 26/26 ('--no-build deploys only a Worker built from the checked-out commit' fails when builtFromRefusal ignores the commit); //crates/clax-worker:deploy_lib_test PASSED in just test-affected main; a scratch copy of cloudflare-setup.sh with stub install scripts prints 'skipped (--no-build: ...)' and runs neither stub under --no-build; actionlint passes.","supersedes":"24dc2571e2b22b992aae0effd6cc7c5bb6fc7cf4f5d0eb2146eadf4c336f7eaa","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/deploy-prod.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T20:08:22.477300Z","id":"285db4d5ca716b9e41705fc3f8028cd61d909300445fc35a4308a54e3a69977a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d74f69221","summary":"Fixed: deploy.mjs keeps the 'Current Version ID: <UUID>' wrangler deploy prints (deploy-lib.mjs versionIdOf) in the record's version_id, dropping an earlier deploy's, and the Summary step of .github/workflows/deploy-prod.yml prints it as 'Cloudflare version'. Evidence: node --test crates/clax-worker/deploy-lib.test.mjs passes 27/27 ('the version ID is the one wrangler deploy names as current' fails when versionIdOf returns null); //crates/clax-worker:deploy_lib_test PASSED in just test-affected main; the Summary step's field reader, run on a record {build, version_id, owner_token}, prints the build and the version ID and nothing for a missing record; actionlint passes. The wrangler output format is taken from wrangler 4's deploy output, not from a real deploy here.","supersedes":"0932d6a221651f3b40f3420b68c7415e46371cf5732a99baad99c5280a4a6c80","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/deploy-prod.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T20:08:52.815682Z","id":"d230d2881872b67f7fdb595a5d38755019d2cac8e6e7a7d5b7d2bed972a5f27b","body":{"detail":"The Build step has no secret in its environment, but it runs in the same job as the Deploy step, so a package install script or crate build script could change files the Deploy step then runs with CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN (the checkout, crates/clax-worker/node_modules/.bin/wrangler, target/tools). A separate build job uploading web/dist and crates/clax-worker/build as an artifact, and a deploy job that installs only wrangler (npm ci --ignore-scripts, if wrangler runs without its install scripts) would close that; it is a larger change than the step split and untried.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":78},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"e590f3314ee4e1e67b54f70a293cf8923173321f8c74b481740da626683b3507"},"summary":"Build in a job of its own and hand only the built files to the deploy job","tags":["security","revisit:a dependency of web/ or crates/clax-worker is found tampering with files at install or build time, or the deploy token's scope widens","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
